{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"functional morality functional morality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md","fileName":"Functional Morality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Functional Morality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Machine Moral Status]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Artificial Moral Agent","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"functional morality functional morality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md","fileName":"Functional Morality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Functional Morality","heading":"Functional Morality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Functional morality is morally acceptable machine behavior achieved without claiming that the machine is a complete moral person. A system can be designed to respect constraints, avoid foreseeable harm, remain within the law, or choose among limited actions using encoded priorities.\n\nThis is a practical target for an [[Artificial Moral Agent]] because safety does not require proving consciousness, emotion, or free will. Its limits matter: a functional system may fail outside the situations anticipated by its designers, and its rule-following does not make it responsible for the values chosen. Human oversight and [[Algorithmic Accountability]] remain necessary.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Artificial Moral Agent","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"functional morality functional morality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Functional Morality.md","fileName":"Functional Morality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Functional Morality","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Artificial Moral Agent","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}